[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Italian Game"]
[Variation "Anti-Fried Liver Defence"]
[ECO "C50"]
[Character "solid,positional"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "solid-centre,slow-build"]
[For "white"]
[Kind "sideline"]
[Opponent "3...h6"]
[Start "giuoco-piano 3.Bc4"]

3... h6 4. c3 { Prepares d4. Black spent a move on h6, so there is no hurry and White can build a strong centre. } 4... Nf6 ( 4... Bc5 5. d4 { Hits the bishop and takes the centre now that Black has not castled. } 5... exd4 6. cxd4 Bb6 ( 6... Bb4+ 7. Nc3 { Blocks the check with a developing move. } 7... Nf6 8. d5 { Hits the knight on c6. If Black takes on c3, bxc3 gives White a big pawn centre. } 8... Bxc3+ 9. bxc3 Na5 10. Bd3 { The bishop is safe from the knight. Plan: castle and push the centre pawns. } ) 7. O-O { Castles. White has the big centre Black gave up with ...exd4. } 7... d6 8. h3 { Stops ...Bg4, which would pin the knight and hit d4. Plan: Nc3, Re1 and Be3. } ) ( 4... d6 5. d3 Nf6 { The same position as 4...Nf6 5.d3 d6. } ) ( 4... a6 5. d3 Nf6 { The same position as 4...Nf6 5.d3 a6. } ) 5. d3 { Guards e4 and keeps the position calm. } 5... d6 ( 5... Bc5 { The same position as the Giuoco Piano 3...Bc5 4.c3 Nf6 5.d3 h6, where White castles. } ) ( 5... d5 6. exd5 Nxd5 7. O-O { Castles. Black's e5 pawn is loose, and Re1 next puts pressure on it. } ) ( 5... a6 6. O-O d6 7. Bb3 { Steps out of reach of ...b5 and keeps aiming at f7. } ) ( 5... Be7 6. O-O d6 { The same position as 5...d6 6.O-O Be7. } ) 6. O-O { Gets the king safe. } 6... Be7 7. Re1 { Defends e4 so the knight on f3 is free to move. Plan: Nbd2, Nf1 and Ng3, then d4 when the pieces are ready. } *
